      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, thanks. that's helpful. \n\nso if it's grubs or nematodes, that's one thing. but what if it's not an animal? i was reading an article about \"microbial activity\" and how certain things in the soil can \"sequestrate\" or just basically trap nutrients so they aren't bioavailable. \n\nit felt a bit weird since they used words like \"stealing\" and \"hoarding\" to describe the process. what's actually happening there? is there anything in the soil that acts like it's actively hiding or hoarding the nitrogen away from the roots?",
